    {
      "title": "Training: optimize only the chosen specialist",
      "explanation": "Bb receives x and zb and produces the symbolic prediction ŷb, which the local objective compares with y. Only the chosen block needs differentiation for this example. The objective and representation depend on the task: continuous-target denoising uses its weighted reconstruction loss, while classification and token adaptations use cross-entropy. No upstream block output is required to obtain this training pair.",
