    {
      "title": "Inference: continue the shared reverse process",
      "explanation": "The next numerical update changes the persistent sampler state from z1 to z2 using Blo’s estimate. Training blocks could acquire their noisy inputs independently from supervised targets; inference states instead depend successively on preceding numerical updates. The noise-indexed specialization therefore removes upstream activation dependence from training without removing sequential state dependence from sampling.",
